course: dictionary
lesson: 11871
title: Bostonian
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A Bostonian is a person who comes from or lives in Boston, a big city in Massachusetts, USA. Look for the clue: the word starts with Boston, so it names people from that place. Like Londoner or Parisian, it tells you where someone is from.
explain: «The Bostonians walked down to the harbour to watch the ships.» Here Bostonians are people, so the word is a noun. Now read «The Bostonian accent is easy to hear.» Here Bostonian describes the accent, so it is an adjective.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Sam is a Bostonian» becomes «Sam is a person from Boston», and it still makes sense. That is how you know your guess is right.
fact: A Bostonian is a person from Boston, a big city in Massachusetts, USA.
fact: As a noun: a Bostonian, Bostonians. As an adjective: Bostonian, as in a Bostonian accent.
fact: In 1773, Bostonians took part in the Boston Tea Party, protesting British taxes by throwing tea into the harbour.
fact: The Boston Tea Party came before the American Revolution.
fact: A Bostonian accent often drops the «r» sound, so «park the car» sounds like «pahk the cah».
exercise: «Mia is a Bostonian, so she lives in Boston.» What is a Bostonian? | *A person who comes from or lives in Boston | A type of boat | A town in England | A cup of tea
exercise: In «The Bostonian accent is easy to hear», which word describes the accent? | the | sounds | *Bostonian | is
exercise: What happened at the Boston Tea Party in 1773? | *Bostonians protested British taxes by throwing tea into the harbour | Bostonians planted tea gardens | Bostonians held a big tea party with cakes | People sailed to Boston to buy tea
test: «The Bostonians walked to the harbour to protest.» What is a Bostonian? | A kind of tea | A famous painter | A large harbour boat | *A person from Boston
test: A Bostonian accent says «pahk the cah» for «park the car». Which sound is missing? | The m sound | The l sound | The t sound | *The r sound
exam: «Our teacher, a Bostonian, told us about the Boston Tea Party in 1773.» Which year was the Boston Tea Party? | 1776 | *1773 | 1673 | 1873
